From: atomchild411 <143453386+atomchild411@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] WTF: IRIX native builds report IRIX64

Cross builds name the system IRIX; CMake on IRIX itself takes uname -s,
which is IRIX64 on 64-bit kernels.  Match both.
---
 Source/WTF/wtf/PlatformWPE.cmake | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Source/WTF/wtf/PlatformWPE.cmake b/Source/WTF/wtf/PlatformWPE.cmake
--- a/Source/WTF/wtf/PlatformWPE.cmake
+++ b/Source/WTF/wtf/PlatformWPE.cmake
@@ -79,7 +79,7 @@
 )
 
 # Real-time threads are Linux's (rtkit over D-Bus, eventfd).
-if (CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME STREQUAL "IRIX")
+if (CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME MATCHES "^IRIX")
     list(REMOVE_ITEM WTF_SOURCES linux/RealTimeThreads.cpp)
 endif ()
 
